cedonian Empire was the empire created by Alexander the Great, who conquered the Achaemenid Empire and reached as far as the Indus between 334 and 323 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-front"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/macedonian-front.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Macedonian front</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 1915–1918</span><span class="enc-snip">The Macedonian front, also called the Salonika front, was a theatre of the First World War in northern Greece and southern Serbia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/macedonians-ethnic-group"><span class="enc-name">Macedonians (ethnic group)</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Macedonians, in the modern sense, are a South Slavic people of the region of Macedonia in the southern Balkans.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/machado-de-assis"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/machado-de-assis.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Machado de Assis</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Machado de Assis was a Brazilian novelist, short-story writer and poet, widely regarded as the greatest writer in Brazilian literature.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/machanidas"><span class="enc-name">Machanidas</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Machanidas was ruler of Sparta from about 211 BCE, governing in the name of the boy king Pelops.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/machares"><span class="enc-name">Machares</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Machares was a son of Mithridates VI of Pontus who governed the Bosporan Kingdom as his father's viceroy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/machchhu-river"><img 